  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="AT3G07270-CPLX" textLabel="AT3G07270-CPLX" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G07270-CPLX" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>Four classes of GTP cyclohydrolases are currrently known: |FRAME: FOLE-CPLX GTP cyclohydrolase I| converts GTP to |FRAME: DIHYDRONEOPTERIN-P3 7,8-dihydroneopterin 3&apos;-triphosphate|, the first step in the biosynthesis of folate. |FRAME: GTP-CYCLOHYDRO-II-CPLX GTP cyclohydrolase II| converts GTP to |FRAME: DIAMINO-OH-PHOSPHORIBOSYLAMINO-PYR 2,5-diamino-6-(5-phospho-D-ribosylamino)pyrimidin-4(3H)-one|, the first step in the bacterial and eukaryotic pathways for flavin biosynthesis. |FRAME: CPLX-7773 GTP cyclohydrolase III| converts GTP to |FRAME: CPD-10808 2-amino-5-formylamino-6-(5-phospho-D-ribosylamino)pyrimidin-4(3H)-one|, the first step in the archaeal pathways for flavin biosynthesis. |FRAME: CPLX-7774 GTP cyclohydrolase IV| converts GTP to |FRAME: CPD-10812 7,8-dihydroneopterin 2&apos;,3&apos;-cyclic phosphate|, an early intermediate to pterins in archaea. &lt;b&gt;About This Enzyme&lt;/b&gt; The GTP cyclohydrolase I (GCHI) from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; was identified by using the protein sequence of the |FRAME:TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;| and mammalian GCHI. The functionality of the enzyme was proven by complementing a yeast &lt;i&gt;fol2&lt;/i&gt; mutant and by demonstrating the enzyme activity in extracts of comlemented yeast. The GCHI cDNA was shown to encode a unique bimodular enzyme. The GCHI is a dimer with subunits of about 50 kDa and consists of two GCHI-like domains in tandem. Both domains are necessary to present the functional protein. The transit sequence in GCHI indicates a cytosolic location of the enzyme |CITS: [12221287]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G07270-CPLX" />
